markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Computer Systems and Devices Curriculum Overview
 
This unit introduces students to AI and computing systems, emphasizing how they process information, integrate with emerging technologies, and impact society.

Through hands-on activities and discussions, students design and troubleshoot systems, analyze AI’s ethical implications, and apply human-centered design to create equitable, technology-driven solutions.


<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);  font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 800px; margin: 20px auto;">

  <div>
    <p>Students will:</p>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14pt">
      <li> Explain how AI and computing systems process information and interact with hardware and software.</li>&#8201;
    <li> Design, troubleshoot, and optimize computing systems while exploring emerging technologies like IoT and robotics.</li>&#8201;
    <li> Apply human-centered design principles to develop AI-driven solutions for real-world problems.</li><br>
    <li> Critically evaluate AI-generated outputs for accuracy, reliability, and potential biases.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div>
    <img src="https://images.code.org/39c4021c9dc61fc1544c823039aed657-image-1741880050858.png" 
         alt="Icon with computer and gears" 
         style="border-radius: 10px; width: 300px; height: auto;">
  </div>
</div>

<p style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; display: inline-block;">
    ➡️ Explore the entire unit <a href='https://studio.code.org/s/aif3-2025' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>here</a>.
</p>

<div style="clear:both;"></div>

---

## Unit Calendar 

Here is a quick overview of the lessons in this unit. 

This version of the calendar shows the pacing for 45 minute class periods and can be customized using the drop-down menu to accommodate your schedule. 

Check out the <a href="https://studio.code.org/s/aif3-2025" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">calendar feature</a> on top of the unit preview. 


